# Copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is git-ignored: never commit it.
# The scripts source it when it exists.

IMAGE=swift-tensorfold:local
MODEL=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4

HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8083
NAME=swift-1.5

# Host directories. The checkpoint is 186 GB; the image another 40 GB.
HF_DIR=$HOME/.cache/swift-tensorfold/hf        # Hugging Face cache (the checkpoint lands here)
STATE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/swift-tensorfold/state  # triton/torch kernel caches, prefix snapshots
MODELS_DIR=$HOME/models                        # optional local checkpoints, mounted read-only

# Only needed when Hugging Face asks for it (gated or rate-limited access). Leave empty to stay anonymous.
HF_TOKEN=

# The lanes and the window: three lanes of the checkpoint's native 262144 (4799 MiB a lane, int8 KV), the
# configuration the README's numbers were taken with. PARALLEL is worth setting: the server's own default decodes
# one request at a time and queues the rest, so N sessions cost N times the wall time.
PARALLEL=3
CONTEXT=262144

# Extra `tensorfold serve` flags, word-split as they are here. Options that matter on 128 GB:
#   EXTRA_ARGS="--ple-on-ssd"                   # n-gram tables stay on disk: ~40 GiB less peak
#   EXTRA_ARGS="--ple-on-ssd --ssd-experts 90"  # plus routed experts streamed into a 90 GiB pool
#   EXTRA_ARGS="--mtp-drafts 6"                 # MTP drafts a round (the CUDA default; 0 disables)
#   EXTRA_ARGS="--no-drafts"                    # serial reference, for a baseline
#   EXTRA_ARGS="--no-thinking"                  # skip the reasoning pass (a shorter reply, less quality)
# Quote the value when it has multiple flags so `set -a; . .env` does not execute them.
EXTRA_ARGS="--thinking --reasoning-effort xhigh --vision --max-tokens 32768 --kv-dtype int8 --mtp-confidence 0.60"

# 8-bit copies of the BF16 dense faces, read instead of the rows (the README's "8-bit dense faces"). `all` is the
# rig's reference arm; upstream declines the trade, so it is this branch's own knob.
TENSORFOLD_FACES_FP8=all

# The vision tower's workspace reserve, in MiB, counted against the startup admission. The engine's own default
# is 4096 (unchanged through 0.6.2); this rig measured 0.76 GiB for a 4M-pixel image and 0.83 GiB for a video, so
# it reserves 1280.
TENSORFOLD_VISION_WORKSPACE_MIB=1280

# Build another revision of the fork (a commit sha or a branch name). The Dockerfile already defaults to
# TF_REPO=https://github.com/tournierjc/TensorFold.git and the pinned integration/0.6.2 commit; pass TF_REPO
# too when pointing at another repository (upstream, for a baseline).
TF_REF=d26e09fbd723f73dba84b6c6c4c2b0816ce98c10

# A second arm of the same family, served from a *directory* rather than a repo id. bench/arms.json lists
# them, scripts/pull-arm.sh fills one, and scripts/preflight-arm.sh sizes one before it is loaded. The window
# is granted per arm: four lanes at the native 262144 fit this one (77.92 GiB of 104.76), where the 186 GB
# NVFP4 arm refuses the fourth. STATE_DIR is per arm so that one arm's kernel caches and prefix snapshots can
# never be read by another - the price is a slower first load, because the kernels compile again.
#
#   IMAGE=swift-tensorfold:063-d31685e            # the integration head that names the EXL3 vision sidecar
#   MODEL=/models/exl3-405                        # a path under MODELS_DIR, not ukisai/...
#   PARALLEL=4
#   STATE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/swift-tensorfold/state-exl3-405
#   TENSORFOLD_VISION_WEIGHTS=/models/exl3-405/vision-f16.safetensors
#
# and TENSORFOLD_FACES_FP8 left unset: 8-bit dense faces are copies of the BF16 faces an EXL3 pack does not
# have, so the knob is inert there and only makes the profile lie about what is being served.

# Crash diagnosis. TORCH_USE_CUDA_DSA=1 (a device-side assert names the faulting kernel),
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True (fragmentation), CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1
# (serialised launches; keep off while graphs are captured). Forwarded only when set.
TORCH_USE_CUDA_DSA=0

# Set to 1 to skip prompt-kernel warm on first serve (Spark NVFP4 MoE IMA workaround while iterating).
# First real request pays the warm cost instead.
# TENSORFOLD_SKIP_WARM=1

# Optional MoE backend override (grouped default; python = host item loop):
# TENSORFOLD_NVFP4_MOE=grouped
